TITLE:: Metronome
SUMMARY:: A simple metronome
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/Sequencer, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/SequencerGui

DESCRIPTION::
This class plays short bursts of noise on the beat of LINK::Classes/TempoClock#*default::, and quieter bursts on the offbeats.

NOTE::
The metronome depends on the server running.
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: isPlaying
Whether the metronome LINK::Classes/Pdef:: is currently playing.

RETURNS::
CODE::true:: or CODE::false::.

METHOD:: play
Starts playing the metronome. If the server is not running, boots it via LINK::Classes/Setup:: and starts playback when boot completes.

NOTE::
As this method will add the LINK::Classes/SynthDef:: TELETYPE::\metronome:: if it hasn't already, there could conceivably be a delay or some warnings to the post window while this is happening.
::

METHOD:: stop
Stops the metronome.

METHOD:: toggle
Starts the metronome if it is not playing; otherwise stops it. See LINK::#-play:: and LINK::#-stop::.

METHOD:: volume
The metronome playback volume, between 0 and 1. The default is 0.5. Setting clips the new value to that range.

ARGUMENT:: newValue
The new volume when setting.

RETURNS::
The current volume.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
// Start the server
Setup.server;

// Play the metronome
Metronome.play;

// Make it quieter
Metronome.volume_(0.1);

// Stop it
Metronome.stop;
::
